ight cache daemon parent process.\r\n\r\nThe endpoint reports `starting` while daemon ranks are loading, `ready` after all expected target and draft ranks are available, and `failed` if a daemon process exits. This allows external service management systems to distinguish daemon startup from readiness.\r\n\r\nStacked on #58370. Will rebase once #58370 is merged.\r\n\r\ncc: @Isotr0py @liusy58\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nTest `tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_weight_cache.py` with both target-only and target-plus-draft configurations.\r\n\r\nVerify that the daemon reports the expected health state after all ranks are ready, and that IPC weight loading and generation complete successfully.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nThe tests confirm correct health reporting and successful IPC weight loading for both configurations.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":6579171167,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABiCYvXw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","description":"","color":"80D2AC","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7197733874,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABrQSz8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/ready","name":"ready","description":"ONLY add when PR is ready to merge/full CI is needed","color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T12:11:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T03:55:01Z","closed_a